WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:11.071
Clio-X is a place where archives share records for research, including research with AI.

2
00:00:11.072 --> 00:00:16.274
The key idea: researchers can analyse records without taking a copy home.

3
00:00:17.899 --> 00:00:24.934
The screens are also available in Japanese.

4
00:00:30.457 --> 00:00:35.990
Each dataset has its own page, much like an entry in a catalogue.

5
00:00:37.608 --> 00:00:42.809
It names who holds the records: here, the University of British Columbia.

6
00:00:44.464 --> 00:00:49.665
It gets a persistent identifier, like a reference code that never changes.

7
00:00:51.279 --> 00:00:57.145
Every change to the description is logged with its date, like an audit trail.

8
00:00:58.757 --> 00:01:02.957
This dataset is marked "compute": it cannot be downloaded.

9
00:01:04.573 --> 00:01:09.106
Instead, an analysis is run inside a closed "data room".

10
00:01:09.107 --> 00:01:13.641
The researcher receives only the results, never the records themselves.

11
00:01:15.254 --> 00:01:22.121
This dataset is free. A small network fee still applies, and the page says so up front.

12
00:01:23.739 --> 00:01:26.740
Looking around needs no account.

13
00:01:26.741 --> 00:01:32.276
A wallet (a digital signing key) is needed only to run an analysis.
